    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1725">

                <pb facs="1233" n="1117" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1117"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.812/131.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Long to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s April 4. The President expressed gratification that our Government
                    was disposed to consider favorably his [omission in <pb facs="1234" n="1118"
                        xml:id="pg1118"/> transmission]. * * * While discussing in some detail the
                    school, he expressed the opinion that all Central America should enjoy the
                    privilege of entering its students under certain rules and regulations.</p>
                <p>He made clear, however, that his first and greatest desire was to see Salvador
                    put on a gold basis, and thought the matter could be arranged. * * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
